'''Soul Ripper''' is a [[unique]] {{il|Quartz Flask}}.

== Interactions ==

=== % Reduced Flask Charge Used ===
The Vaal Souls gained are will be the actual flask charges used. So if you have a 100 flask version and you have 15% reduced flask charges used you will gain 85 Vaal Souls. 

=== % Chance of flask not using charges ===
This will gain you souls even when no charges are used.

=== % Increased Flask Effect ===
Increased flask effect will not increase the Vaal Souls gained.

=== Multiple Vaal Skills ===
Souls can be allocated to multiple Vaal skills. 

If you have 2 Vaal skills with zero souls, and a 60 charges/souls flask, the souls will be shared between both skills, so you'll get near 30 souls for each.

With one full Vaal skill, and one empty Vaal skill, the souls go only to the empty skill.

{{Item acquisition}}

==Ruthless mode==
Utility Flasks cannot gain charges while active in [[Ruthless mode]]. This flask also has a flask duration of 4.00 seconds instead.

==Legacy variants==
Soul Ripper has a [[legacy variant]].

{{legacy variant table header}}
{{legacy variant table row|3.10.0|
* {{c|mod|100% increased Charges used}}
* {{c|mod|Vaal Skills deal (30-40)% more Damage during Effect}}
* {{c|mod|Vaal Skills used during effect do not apply Soul Gain Prevention}}
* {{c|mod|Gains no Charges during effect of any Soul Ripper Flask}}
}}
{{Legacy variant table end}}

Even using a legacy {{il|Soul Catcher}}, the [[Altar of Sacrifice]] will upgrades the item to the current variant of Soul Ripper, instead of the legacy version.

